{# GETTING HERE — the illustrated regional map in a frame, drive times, GO Transit, the two region descriptions (rewritten to grade 5–7 from the client copy; facts kept). #}
<section class="section {{ hereField or 'field--night' }}" id="getting-here" data-module="map">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head"><h2>Getting here</h2><p>St. Catharines and the Benchlands are an easy winter drive from across the Golden Horseshoe, and you can leave the car at home: <a class="tlink" href="https://www.gotransit.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-module="map" data-card-label="GO Transit">GO Transit</a> runs train and bus service to St. Catharines.</p></div>
    {% if slots.widgets.GETTING_HERE_MAP.embed %}
    <figure class="print region-map">
      <span class="print__mat">
        <picture>
          <source srcset="{{ slots.widgets.GETTING_HERE_MAP.embed | replace('.png', '.webp') }}" type="image/webp">
          <img class="print__img" src="{{ slots.widgets.GETTING_HERE_MAP.embed }}" width="1600" height="1034" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
               alt="Illustrated map of St. Catharines and the Niagara Benchlands along Lake Ontario, from Beamsville, Vineland and Jordan in the west to Port Dalhousie and downtown St. Catharines in the east, with the QEW, the Bruce Trail, the Waterfront Trail and the wine route marked.">
        </picture>
      </span>
    </figure>
    {% endif %}
    <div class="here-grid">
      <div>
        <h3>Drive times</h3>
        <ul class="drive">
          {% for o in site.gettingHere.origins %}<li><b>{{ o.from }}</b><span>{{ o.time }} · {{ o.note }}</span></li>{% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Niagara Benchlands</h3>
        <p class="region-copy">The Niagara Benchlands sit on the slopes of the Escarpment between Beamsville, Vineland and Jordan. More than 50 wineries make wine here, and in winter many of them pour icewine by the fire. Add orchards, farm markets, small villages and the Bruce Trail along the UNESCO Escarpment, and you have a day that mixes a good lunch with a good walk.</p>
        <h3>St. Catharines</h3>
        <p class="region-copy">St. Catharines is the city side of the region. Downtown has the restaurants, craft breweries, shops and the FirstOntario Performing Arts Centre within a few blocks. Port Dalhousie has the lake, the pier and the old carousel. In winter the streets are lit, the museums are warm, and the Bruce Trail and the canal paths are a short drive away.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{% set hereField = "" %}
